---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import CategoryHub from '../../../../components/CategoryHub.astro';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  const categories = [
    {
      slug: 'testing-workflow',
      category: 'Testing Guide',
      title: 'Testing Workflow & Reports — Sanshi Bio',
      description: 'Pigeon sample collection, shipping, testing workflow, report interpretation and re-test boundaries.',
      bannerTitle: 'Testing Workflow & Reports',
      bannerDescription: 'From sample to report: quality control, interpretation and the next decision.',
      breadcrumb: 'Testing Guide',
      serviceHref: '/en/services/',
      serviceLabel: 'View testing services',
      intro: [
        'A test is not “send a sample and wait for a sheet.” The value of a report depends on whether the sample is traceable, whether the test matches the question, whether the report is read correctly, and whether the result changes the next decision.',
        'This hub follows the chain: sampling and sample quality, shipping and chain of custody, laboratory testing and controls, report interpretation and re-testing. Each step can change the conclusion; the laboratory is not the only place where quality is made.',
        'If this is your first test, start with sample collection and report interpretation. If you already have a result that does not fit the clinical picture, read the false-negative/false-positive guide before ordering another test.',
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: 'pathogen-health',
      category: 'Virus Control',
      title: 'Pathogens & Health — Sanshi Bio',
      description: 'Pigeon virus, bacterial and parasite testing, loft health and the boundary between evidence and diagnosis.',
      bannerTitle: 'Pathogens & Health',
      bannerDescription: 'From pathogen detection to loft management: a result is evidence, not the end of diagnosis.',
      breadcrumb: 'Virus Control',
      serviceHref: '/en/virus-detection/',
      serviceLabel: 'View virus detection',
      intro: [
        'Health problems in racing pigeons are rarely explained by one pathogen alone. Viruses, bacteria, parasites, environmental stress and management can overlap; the same positive report can mean something different with different signs, groups and sampling times.',
        'This hub focuses on three questions: when testing is worth doing, what a result can actually support, and who should make the next call. Laboratory results belong inside clinical signs, epidemiology and veterinary judgement, not in place of them.',
        'Start with the pathogen closest to the current signs. If the result and the clinical picture disagree, read the false-negative/false-positive and re-testing material before expanding treatment.',
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: 'flight-genetics',
      category: 'Flight Genes',
      title: 'Flight Genetics — Sanshi Bio',
      description: 'Pigeon endurance, homing, navigation and muscle genes: scientific interpretation and breeding limits.',
      bannerTitle: 'Flight Genetics',
      bannerDescription: 'Genes give direction; training and environment decide expression. Potential is not performance.',
      breadcrumb: 'Flight Genes',
      serviceHref: '/en/flight-ability/',
      serviceLabel: 'View flight-gene testing',
      intro: [
        'Flight ability is not controlled by one gene. LDHA, DRD4, CRY1, MSTN and other markers can suggest a direction, but endurance, homing, navigation and muscle power also depend on training, health, nutrition, weather and race conditions.',
        'The purpose of this hub is not to turn a gene report into a champion prediction. It is to explain what a marker can suggest, what cannot be inferred from one marker, and how to place genetic information beside pedigree, race record and offspring data.',
        'For a first report, start with gene interactions and polygenic limits. Before pairing, read genetics versus training. If the report and the race record disagree, exclude management, health and sample problems first.',
      ],
    },
    {
      slug: 'bloodline-identity',
      category: 'Bloodline',
      title: 'Bloodline & Identity — Sanshi Bio',
      description: 'Pigeon paternity testing, gene ID cards, AB detection, sex identification and the evidence chain.',
      bannerTitle: 'Bloodline & Identity',
      bannerDescription: 'A bloodline is not a piece of paper: connect sample, markers, probability and transaction evidence.',
      breadcrumb: 'Bloodline',
      serviceHref: '/en/paternity/',
      serviceLabel: 'View paternity testing',
      intro: [
        'The point of a paternity test is not a prettier percentage. It is whether the sample can be attributed, whether the marker panel is adequate, how the probability is calculated, and whether the report can be reviewed in a sale or registration.',
        'This hub covers parentage, gene ID cards, AB detection and sex identification. We keep “exclusion” separate from “support,” probability separate from certainty, and the laboratory report separate from a pedigree or transaction record.',
        'If you are buying or selling a bird, start with the sample chain and SNP-panel limits. If you are building an identity record, start with the gene ID card and sampling workflow.',
      ],
    },
  ];
  return categories.map((category) => ({ params: { category: category.slug }, props: category }));
}

const category = Astro.props;
const posts = (await getCollection('blogEn'))
  .filter((post) => post.data.category === category.category)
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.pubDate.valueOf() - a.data.pubDate.valueOf());
---

<CategoryHub
  title={category.title}
  description={category.description}
  bannerTitle={category.bannerTitle}
  bannerDescription={category.bannerDescription}
  breadcrumb={category.breadcrumb}
  intro={category.intro}
  posts={posts}
  base="/en"
  lang="en"
  serviceHref={category.serviceHref}
  serviceLabel={category.serviceLabel}
/>
